    "body": "Hey, thanks a lot for this amazing work. \n\nHow do I map the segmentation to correct id? What are the paramters used for hls_pallete? I tried to follow the code and I noticed the `hls_palette` function is used to generate the colors using `pallette = plotting.hls_palette(len(assets) + 2)`. However, this is not generating the right colors. \n\nFor example : The scene val/r1_new_f has 32 assets. The pallete generate from this does not match the colors in the segmentation mask. I also noticed all of the images in this scene only have 31 unique colors (combined) instead of 34. Morevover, for some reason the scene.json also has background twice! \n\nColors in the segmentation masks \n`[[  0   0   0]\n [ 38  57 217]\n [ 38  87 217]\n [ 38 117 217]\n [ 38 147 217]\n [ 38 176 217]\n [ 38 206 217]\n [ 38 217  49]\n [ 38 217  79]\n [ 38 217 108]\n [ 38 217 138]\n [ 38 217 168]\n [ 38 217 198]\n [ 49  38 217]\n [ 57 217  38]\n [ 79  38 217]\n [ 87 217  38]\n [108  38 217]\n [117 217  38]\n [138  38 217]\n [147 217  38]\n [168  38 217]\n [176 217  38]\n [198  38 217]\n [206 217  38]\n [217  38 117]\n [217  38 147]\n [217  38 176]\n [217  38 206]\n [217 168  38]\n [217 198  38]]\n`\nColors from the pallete function \n`[[  0,   0,   0],\n       [ 38,  49, 217],\n       [ 38,  80, 217],\n       [ 38, 112, 217],\n       [ 38, 143, 217],\n       [ 38, 175, 217],\n       [ 38, 206, 217],\n       [ 38, 196, 217],\n       [ 38, 164, 217],\n       [ 38, 133, 217],\n       [ 38, 101, 217],\n       [ 38,  70, 217],\n       [ 38,  38, 217],\n       [ 38,  70, 217],\n       [ 38, 101, 217],\n       [ 38, 133, 217],\n       [ 38, 164, 217],\n       [ 38, 196, 217],\n       [ 38, 206, 217],\n       [ 38, 175, 217],\n       [ 38, 143, 217],\n       [ 38, 112, 217],\n       [ 38,  80, 217],\n       [ 38,  49, 217],\n       [ 38,  59, 217],\n       [ 38,  91, 217],\n       [ 38, 122, 217],\n       [ 38, 154, 217],\n       [ 38, 185, 217],\n       [ 38, 217, 217],\n       [ 38, 185, 217],\n       [ 38, 154, 217],\n       [ 38, 122, 217],\n       [ 38,  91, 217],\n       [ 38,  59, 217]]`\n\nscene.json\n`{\"sensor_width\": 50.0, \"sensor_height\": 24.0, \"focal_length\": 30.0, \"assets\": [\"background\", \"background\", \"model\", \"model.001\", \"model.002\", \"model.003\", \"model.004\", \"model.005\", \"model.006\", \"new-2.001\", \"new-2.004\", \"new-5.002\", \"new-6.003\", \"new-7.001\", \"original-1.001\", \"original-15\", \"original-8\", \"r1_Chest\", \"r1_Head\", \"r1_LeftArm\", \"r1_LeftFoot\", \"r1_LeftForeArm\", \"r1_LeftHand\", \"r1_LeftLeg\", \"r1_LeftUpperLeg\", \"r1_RightArm\", \"r1_RightFoot\", \"r1_RightForeArm\", \"r1_RightHand\", \"r1_RightLeg\", \"r1_RightUpperLeg\", \"r1_Waist\"], \"character\": \"r1\"}`\n\nAny idea how to solve this or what am I doing wrong? \n\nRegards, \nDivyam ",
