    "body": "Thank you for providing this excellent dataset!\r\n\r\nI have a few questions on the trajs_3d array in the annotation files. As I understand, trajs_3d has a shape of (S, N, 3), and I’d like to confirm some details:\r\n\r\n1. Does the first axis (S) represent time steps, and the second axis (N) represent point indices?\r\n2. Are the 3D coordinates provided in world coordinates, or are they in a different reference frame?\r\n3. I noticed that the value of N is smaller than the total number of pixels (H*W). What's the criteria used for selecting these points as keypoints?\r\n\r\nThank you very much for your time and assistance!",
    "closed_by": {
      "login": "yuantianyuan01",
      "id": 45124314,
