    "issue_dependencies_summary": {
      "blocked_by": 0,
      "total_blocked_by": 0,
      "blocking": 0,
      "total_blocking": 0
    },
    "body": "Hi,\r\n\r\nThanks for the useful work on this dataset!\r\n\r\nI was wondering about the scale of the depth maps provided in the dataset, specifically the `depths/*.png` files. It seems that when reading out (e.g. https://github.com/aharley/pips2/blob/master/datasets/pointodysseydataset_3d.py#L172, https://github.com/y-zheng18/point_odyssey/blob/main/utils/reprojection.py#L88) you scale based on the uint16 range, and then multiply by 1000.\r\n\r\nIs this to get the depth of each pixel in millimeters, as distance from the camera?\r\n\r\nAll the best,\r\nSkanda",
    "closed_by": {
      "login": "skoppula",
      "id": 1685743,
      "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjE2ODU3NDM=",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1685743?v=4",
