      "total_blocked_by": 0,
      "blocking": 0,
      "total_blocking": 0
    },
    "body": "Hi, how are the extrinsics provided in the dataset supposed to be used? If I want to align, say 10 frames to a global coordinate frame, right now I'm just doing `world_coords = inv(extrinsics) @ camera_coords` but this does not bring all 10 frames into a common frame. I have also tried `world_coords = inv(R2 @ extrinsics @ R1) @ camera_coords` as given in `reprojection.py` but this does not work either. I am not able to find any documentation of the annotations.",
    "closed_by": {
      "login": "tarashakhurana",
      "id": 12378485,
      "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjEyMzc4NDg1",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12378485?v=4",
