    "body": "Hi @y-zheng18 , thanks for your excellent work! I'm trying to generate some sequences for my research with point_odyssey. But I come across some issues when retargeting the motion. \r\n\r\nThe retargeted motion looks like following figures. The retargeted motion is barely smpl-x model without any texture. \r\n![Screenshot from 2023-08-10 16-03-36](https://github.com/y-zheng18/point_odyssey/assets/54616858/c3f7eb06-d307-4db3-bf12-129fb29444d2)\r\n\r\nWhen transferring the fhe fbx module to Blender. I didn't rename the armature but changed the code as flowing:\r\n```[python]\r\n        for i, character in enumerate(character_list):\r\n            character_collection_path = os.path.join(self.character_path, character, 'Collection')\r\n            bpy.ops.wm.append(directory=character_collection_path, filename='Armature')\r\n            skeleton = bpy.data.objects['Armature']\r\n\r\n            self.retarget_smplx2skeleton(skeleton, motion_list[i])\r\n```\r\n\r\nI'm not very familiar with Blender, so I would be extremely grateful if you could provide any suggestions. Thank you in advance.\r\n\r\nBests,\r\nWeining",
