    "body": "Hello and thank you for the amazing dataset! I've been working with the validation set and observed that the `animal2_s` video contains regions with maximum depth values, specifically where there's an emission of smoke from the ground. I've included a GIF below for reference, where the RGB images are presented on the top and the corresponding depth maps on the bottom.\r\n\r\nGiven the nature of smoke and its challenges for RGBD sensors, I'm curious to understand if this is the expected representation in the dataset. Is the smoke intended to be portrayed with an \"infinite\" or maximum depth value in this scenario? I'd appreciate any insights or clarifications on this. Thanks!\r\n\r\n![video.animal2_s.10fps](https://github.com/y-zheng18/point_odyssey/assets/17498813/381c4ffb-0762-427c-9eb5-4c755d163a99)\r\n",
